const PRIVACY = "How information is handled when you use the Application\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains what information is used when you operate the Application, how purchases are managed, and what choices and privacy rights are available to you. The Application is supplied by an individual developer and primarily connects your phone to compatible televisions.\n\n## Data Controller and Contact\n\nKees Prins is the operator of the Application and, where applicable, the controller of personal data described in this policy. Postal address: Vlierboomstraat 10, 3552 BR Utrecht, Netherlands. Privacy and support email: kees@prins.mom.\n\n## Information Used by the Application\n\n### Local network and connected televisions\n\nThe Application requests Local Network access to discover and communicate with compatible televisions. Depending on the connected device and the network, this can involve local network addresses, device discovery details, connection status, and commands needed to operate the television. These details are used for the requested connection and may be kept temporarily on the phone for operation or preferences. We do not operate an independent remote-control backend that receives or stores television-control traffic.\n\n### Microphone and voice search\n\nMicrophone access is requested to support voice search on a television when you activate the relevant microphone control. Spoken input may be transmitted to the connected television or handled by its voice-search system, depending on the device and integration. We do not operate our own speech-recognition server and do not maintain a server archive of microphone recordings. A television manufacturer or its speech provider may process voice-search data under its own policies. You may disable microphone access in your phone’s settings; voice search may then be unavailable.\n\n### Optional media or screen transmission\n\nWhere a casting, file-transmission, or screen-mirroring function is available, content selected by you may be transmitted to a compatible receiving device. The Application does not operate a developer-controlled cloud repository for your photos, videos, files, or mirrored screen content. Access to media is governed by the system features and permissions used to initiate the relevant action. The receiving television or its software may have separate data-handling practices.\n\n### Purchases and Apphud\n\nThe Application uses ApphudSDK to manage subscription entitlements, validate purchase status, prevent purchase-related errors or fraud, and obtain aggregated subscription and revenue statistics. Information processed through Apphud may include a pseudonymous Apphud user identifier, purchase and subscription status, Apple transaction or receipt-related information, app version, operating-system version, device model, locale, time zone, and network information such as an IP address. A device identifier such as IDFV may be processed if the relevant Apphud collection option or integration is enabled. Apphud does not collect the iOS advertising identifier (IDFA) by default; no separate advertising-tracking integration has been identified for the current Application.\n\nPurchases are initiated and billed through Apple. We do not receive your full payment card details. Some transaction data is received or processed by Apple and Apphud to verify the entitlement associated with the Application. Apphud may make purchase-related statistics available to us. We do not use a separate general-purpose analytics service or a separate third-party crash-reporting service based on the current implementation information.\n\n### Support communications\n\nIf you email us for assistance, we receive the email address, message, and any information you choose to include. We use it to respond to your inquiry and to resolve the matter you describe. Please avoid emailing passwords, payment card information, or other unnecessary sensitive information.\n\n## Purposes and Legal Bases\n\nWhere the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) applies, we process information only as needed for a lawful purpose. Device connection information and necessary purchase-entitlement information support performance of the service you request. Subscription administration, service integrity, and proportionate purchase statistics may also serve our legitimate interests in operating and securing the Application, where those interests are not overridden by your rights. Information may be processed to meet legal obligations, including accounting or consumer-protection requirements. Where consent is required, including permission to access the microphone, you can control it using the relevant permission and other available choices.\n\n## Service Providers and Disclosures\n\nWe do not sell personal data. We may share or make information available only when necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including:\n\nApple, for App Store purchases, billing, subscription management, and platform services;\n\nApphud, for purchase validation, entitlement management, and subscription-related analytics;\n\na connected television or its software provider, when you use local-network controls, voice search, or an available content-transmission feature; and\n\ncompetent authorities or professional advisers, where disclosure is legally required or reasonably necessary to protect legal rights.\n\nApphud privacy information: https://legal.apphud.com/privacy . Apple’s privacy information is available through Apple’s official privacy pages. Third-party device manufacturers may provide separate notices for television functions.\n\n## Retention and Deletion\n\nLocal connection information and app preferences remain on your device for as long as needed for the Application to function or as allowed by your device settings. Removing the Application generally removes its local app data, subject to operating-system backups and any information retained separately by the operating system.\n\nSubscription and transaction records managed by Apple and Apphud are not necessarily deleted when you uninstall the Application. These records are held for the periods reasonably required to administer purchases, meet legal obligations, resolve disputes, and prevent fraud, in accordance with the relevant providers’ retention practices. We do not maintain a separate server-side library of your photos, videos, screen recordings, or voice-search recordings. You may request information about personal data or ask for deletion by writing to kees@prins.mom; lawful retention exceptions may apply.\n\n## Security and International Processing\n\nWe take reasonable steps appropriate to the limited data processing described here. Local-network communications depend in part on the security of your home network and connected television. No system is completely secure, and you should use a trusted Wi-Fi network and keep your devices updated.\n\nProviders such as Apphud or Apple may process information in countries other than your own, including outside the European Economic Area. Where required, such processing must be supported by a lawful international-transfer mechanism and applicable safeguards. More information about each provider’s practices is available in its privacy documentation.\n\n## Your Rights and Choices\n\nDepending on applicable law and your circumstances, you may have the right to access, correct, erase, or obtain a copy of personal data; restrict or object to certain processing; withdraw consent where processing relies on consent; and complain to a supervisory authority. To exercise rights concerning information under our control, contact kees@prins.mom. We may need sufficient information to verify and locate relevant records. Requests concerning Apple Account billing information can also be directed to Apple.\n\nYou can disable Local Network or Microphone permission in your device settings, although the corresponding features may stop working. You can manage subscriptions in your Apple Account settings. The Application does not require you to create a separate profile with the developer to use its basic remote functions.\n\n## Children and Families\n\nThe Application is intended for a general audience and does not include a public social network or AI chat feature. Its App Store age rating is not a statement that a child may independently make purchases or consent to any processing where parental authorization is required. We do not knowingly seek personal information from children beyond the data necessary for ordinary app operation and App Store purchases. Parents or guardians may contact us regarding privacy concerns involving a child.\n\n## Advertising, Notifications, and Automated Features\n\nBased on the current version, the Application does not contain third-party advertising, does not provide an AI chat feature, and does not use an independent push-notification, Firebase analytics, or crash-reporting service. Apphud may still process purchase-related technical and usage data as described above. Future changes to services that materially affect personal-data processing will be reflected in an updated policy.\n\n## Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy when the Application, its permissions, service providers, or legal requirements change. The current version will be made available with or through the Application, and we will provide additional notice where required by law. Please review the policy periodically.\n\n## Contact\n\nKees Prins · Vlierboomstraat 10, 3552 BR Utrecht, Netherlands · kees@prins.mom";

const TERMS = "End-user terms for the Application\n\nThese Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern your download, access to, and use of the mobile application made available by Kees Prins (the “Application”). Please read them together with the Privacy Policy. By using the Application, you agree to these Terms to the extent permitted by applicable law.\n\n## Provider and Contact\n\nThe Application is provided by Kees Prins, an individual developer located at Vlierboomstraat 10, 3552 BR Utrecht, Netherlands (“we,” “us,” or “our”). For support, questions, complaints, and legal notices concerning the Application, contact kees@prins.mom.\n\n## Purpose and Functionality\n\nThe Application enables compatible phones to communicate with supported television devices over a local network. Depending on the television model, installed software, network settings, and functionality available in the current version, features may include on-screen remote controls, a text-input interface, and voice-based television search. Media casting, file sharing, or screen mirroring may be available only where expressly offered in the Application and supported by the connected device.\n\nAvailability, performance, and feature support vary by television model, firmware, network environment, and regional device capabilities. We do not guarantee compatibility with every television, operating system, or network configuration.\n\n## Network Access, Microphone, and Content\n\nTo discover and control a television, the Application requires access to the local network. Your phone and television generally need to be connected to the same Wi-Fi network. Denying required network permissions may prevent remote-control functions from working.\n\nThe Application may request microphone permission for voice search on a compatible television. Microphone access is used when you activate the relevant voice-search control, such as holding a microphone button. The processing of spoken commands and availability of voice features may depend on the television manufacturer and its services. You can manage microphone access in the operating system settings.\n\nWhere media-casting or screen-mirroring features are provided, you are responsible for ensuring that you have the rights necessary to display or transmit the selected content. Do not use the Application to infringe copyright, violate another person’s privacy, or access or transmit content unlawfully.\n\n## License to Use the Application\n\nSubject to compliance with these Terms, we grant you a personal, limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the Application on Apple-branded devices that you own or control, as permitted by the Apple Media Services Terms and Conditions and applicable usage rules, including permitted Family Sharing or volume-purchasing arrangements.\n\nYou may not sell, sublicense, redistribute, modify, reverse engineer, interfere with, or exploit the Application or its underlying code, except where such restrictions are prohibited by applicable law. You may not use the Application to disrupt a television, network, or another person’s devices without authorization.\n\n## Subscriptions and In-App Purchases\n\nSome features are available through paid, automatically renewing subscriptions offered through Apple’s in-app purchase system. At present, available subscriptions do not include a free trial. The applicable price, billing period, included features, renewal terms, and any introductory offer (if introduced in a future version) are displayed in the purchase interface before confirmation.\n\nWhen you purchase a subscription, payment is charged by Apple to your Apple Account in accordance with Apple’s terms. Unless you cancel, an auto-renewable subscription renews at the end of each billing period at the rate presented to you, subject to changes and notices required by Apple and applicable law. You can manage or cancel subscriptions in your Apple Account subscription settings. Canceling usually stops future renewals; access ordinarily continues until the end of the paid period, unless Apple’s terms or applicable law provide otherwise.\n\nWe may introduce or discontinue subscription plans, introductory offers, free trials, or one-time in-app purchases in future updates. Such offers are not available unless and until they appear in the Application. Pricing, refunds, payment processing, and eligibility are subject to the App Store purchase terms and applicable consumer law. Contact Apple for App Store billing and refund requests, or email us for assistance concerning access to purchased features.\n\n## Trademark Rights and Brand Authorization\n\nThe onn. name and associated brand elements are trademarks associated with Walmart Apollo, LLC. The developer’s use of these marks in connection with the Application is governed by a separate trademark license and brand authorization agreement with Walmart Apollo, LLC. No right to copy or use these marks is granted to end users under these Terms.\n\nThe Application is developed, published, operated, and supported by Kees Prins. The trademark authorization concerns use of the identified brand elements; it does not mean that Walmart Apollo, LLC, Walmart Inc., or their affiliates operate the Application, provide its customer support, or assume responsibility for its performance. References to other television manufacturers, platforms, or services identify compatibility or third-party technology and remain subject to their respective owners’ rights.\n\n## Third-Party Services and Device Requirements\n\nThe Application may interact with devices, networks, operating-system features, and third-party services that we do not control. Your use of such products and services must comply with the relevant manufacturers’ or providers’ terms. We are not responsible for changes to television firmware, communication protocols, network availability, external services, or third-party content that affect compatibility.\n\n## Intellectual Property\n\nWe and our licensors retain all rights in the Application, its original design, code, and materials, excluding content and rights belonging to third parties. Nothing in these Terms transfers ownership of the Application, television software, third-party content, or any trademark to you.\n\n## Availability, Updates, and Support\n\nWe may update, maintain, change, suspend, or discontinue features as reasonably needed for security, functionality, compatibility, legal compliance, or service operation. We make reasonable efforts to provide the Application as described but do not guarantee uninterrupted operation or that every issue can be resolved. If you experience a problem, contact kees@prins.mom.\n\n## Warranties and Liability\n\nThe Application is provided with the care and skill required by applicable law. To the extent permitted by law, it is otherwise provided “as is” and “as available,” without additional warranties concerning uninterrupted operation, uninterrupted connectivity, or compatibility with every television. Nothing here excludes statutory warranties, remedies, or consumer rights that cannot lawfully be waived.\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses arising from network outages, unsupported devices, third-party services, or misuse of the Application. This provision does not exclude liability for fraud, intentional misconduct, personal injury where non-excludable, or any other liability that cannot legally be limited.\n\n## Suspension and Termination\n\nYou may stop using the Application at any time and delete it from your device. We may restrict access or end the license if you materially violate these Terms, subject to applicable law. Deleting the Application does not automatically cancel an Apple subscription; you must cancel it through the Apple subscription management controls.\n\n## Apple-Specific Provisions\n\nThese Terms are concluded between you and Kees Prins, not Apple. We, not Apple, are solely responsible for the Application and its content, and for maintenance and support. Apple has no obligation to provide maintenance or support services for the Application. To the extent a legally required warranty applies and the Application fails to conform to it, you may notify Apple, which may refund the applicable purchase price; to the fullest extent allowed by law, Apple has no further warranty obligation.\n\nWe, not Apple, are responsible for addressing claims about the Application, including product liability, legal or regulatory compliance, consumer-protection and privacy claims, and claims that the Application or its use infringes third-party intellectual property rights. You represent that you are not located in a country subject to an applicable U.S. embargo or designated as supporting terrorism, and that you are not on any applicable U.S. government prohibited-party list. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them against you.\n\n## Applicable Law and Consumer Rights\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands, without restricting mandatory consumer protections that apply in your country of residence. Any dispute will be handled by a court with jurisdiction under applicable law. Nothing in these Terms limits your right to seek relief from an applicable consumer-protection authority.\n\n## Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may revise these Terms to reflect changes in the Application, legal requirements, or commercial offerings. The current version will be made available with or through the Application. Where required by law, we will provide appropriate notice or obtain consent before material changes take effect. Continued use after an effective change constitutes acceptance only where permitted by law.\n\n## Contact\n\nKees Prins · Vlierboomstraat 10, 3552 BR Utrecht, Netherlands · kees@prins.mom";

